---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import '../styles/blogs.css';
---

<Layout title="Engineering Work — Safu" description="Selected backend, AI, machine learning, and quantitative engineering projects by Safu Harry.">
	<main class="blog-page">
		<Nav />

		<header class="blog-hero">
			<div class="blog-hero__identity">
				<img src="/IMG-20210808-WA0072.jpg" alt="Safu Harry" loading="eager" />
				<div>
					<p class="eyebrow">Engineering Journal · Projects · Architecture</p>
					<h1>Work built from <span>first principles.</span></h1>
				</div>
			</div>
			<p>
				These are not technology demos presented as finished products. They are engineering projects used to
				explore architecture, reliability, security, AI integration, data systems, and reusable software foundations.
			</p>
		</header>

		<section class="project-grid" aria-label="Selected projects">
			<article class="project-card">
				<div class="project-card__meta"><span>01 · Backend Architecture</span><span>Foundation</span></div>
				<h2>FastApiBackbone</h2>
				<p class="project-card__lede">
					A production-oriented, reusable Python backend foundation built around FastAPI. The project addresses the
					engineering concerns that appear after the HTTP layer: configuration, persistence, migrations, lifecycle,
					logging, health checks, dependency boundaries, and testable infrastructure.
				</p>
				<div class="project-card__architecture">FastAPI → API routers → application services
					↓
					repository contracts → infrastructure
					↓
				SQLAlchemy 2.x ↔ PostgreSQL
					↓
				Alembic migrations</div>
				<div class="project-card__tags">
					<span>Python</span><span>FastAPI</span><span>SQLAlchemy 2.x</span><span>PostgreSQL</span><span>Alembic</span><span>Pydantic</span><span>structlog</span><span>Async I/O</span>
				</div>
				<a class="project-card__link" href="https://github.com/safuh/FastApiBackbone" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Inspect the architecture →</a>
			</article>

			<article class="project-card">
				<div class="project-card__meta"><span>02 · AI Systems</span><span>In Progress</span></div>
				<h2>PAssist</h2>
				<p class="project-card__lede">
					A provider-agnostic AI operating platform designed as a durable backend for models, agents, tools,
					retrieval, memory, authenticated users, and future multi-user workspaces. The system treats the AI
					provider as an adapter rather than coupling the application to a single model vendor.
				</p>
				<div class="project-card__architecture">Identity → JWT authentication → sessions
					↓
				FastAPI application → domain modules
					↓
				AI provider contract → Ollama / compatible APIs
					↓
				SQLAlchemy 2.x → Alembic → PostgreSQL</div>
				<div class="project-card__tags">
					<span>Python</span><span>FastAPI</span><span>JWT</span><span>Argon2</span><span>SQLAlchemy</span><span>PostgreSQL</span><span>Ollama</span><span>LLMs</span><span>RAG</span><span>Tool Calling</span>
				</div>
				<a class="project-card__link" href="https://github.com/safuh/Passist" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Explore PAssist →</a>
			</article>
		</section>

		<section class="engineering-note" aria-labelledby="note-title">
			<p class="eyebrow">The connection</p>
			<h2 id="note-title">One foundation, multiple domains.</h2>
			<p>
				FastApiBackbone establishes the reusable backend substrate: asynchronous application structure, database
				lifecycle, migrations, configuration, logging, and clean extension points. PAssist demonstrates how that
				foundation can support a substantially more complex domain with identity, security, AI provider abstraction,
				conversations, tools, documents, memory, and multi-tenancy boundaries.
			</p>
			<p>
				This is the engineering direction behind the rest of the portfolio: build infrastructure that remains stable,
				then compose domain-specific systems on top of it.
			</p>
		</section>

		<footer class="footer">
			<Footer />
		</footer>
	</main>
</Layout>
